      "content": "Testing for an incomplete model requires invoking vulnerabilities that are messy, deeply personal, or illogical. Try posing oblique questions about shared, obscure memories that require nuanced emotional context, rather than just factual data. Introduce deliberately contradictory or highly irrational thought experiments into your conversations to see if the projection can maintain the same level of cognitive dissonance as you can. If the response becomes overly rational or attempts to correct the absurdity, it suggests the underlying simulation lacks true spontaneous unpredictability.",
